messages:
eli: onboarding report: quickstart returns 500 + stack for auth/quota. users confused whether to retry.

sam: example from repro: 
HTTP/1.1 500 Internal Server Error
Content-Type: application/json
{"error":"java.lang.Exception: ...stack..."}

maria: not great. Proposal: immediate sample change to normalize errors into a small typed surface (code + hint + optional retry_after/support_id).

jess: agree. typed enum values (ERR_AUTH, ERR_RATE_LIMIT, ERR_TRANSIENT, ERR_BAD_REQUEST) so SDKs can branch. also ensure JS/Python/Go expose same classes.

eli: sample helper idea (pseudo):
function normalize(resp) {
  if (resp.status===401) return {code:'ERR_AUTH', hint:'refresh token'}
  if (resp.status===429) return {code:'ERR_RATE_LIMIT', retry_after:resp.headers['retry-after']}
  if (resp.status>=500) return {code:'ERR_TRANSIENT', support_id:resp.headers['x-support-id']}
}

maria: infra will stop sending stacks and add x-support-id header. runtime ticket incoming to canonicalize at the edge.

infra-bot: ticket created: RUNTIME-1234 mapping errors at edge.

jess: i'll open a small sample-app PR with normalization and README note about retry/backoff. make SDK change a follow-up but mark as required for next minor.

eli: thanks. this should cut onboarding ticketsdown.
